35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,#### Turn 1 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,- **Jonathan**: The bus rerouting has left the outer wards facing an hour's round trip to reach any staffed counter.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,- **Rin**: The old outreach sheets show forty people showed up every time! That is way more than the main building gets.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The vehicle line overran by a third, yet the equipment allocation closed under budget. The money was there, just misallocated.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The register lists retired tradespeople running the repair clinic, but no one on payroll is trained to supervise outside facilitators.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: The grant only covers twelve months, then the flat budget takes over. That is a very short leash for a new commitment.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, that overrun is worrying. If the vehicle line is already strained, adding a mobile service might just break it further.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"- **Rin**: @Benjamin, wait! If the vehicle broke the budget, maybe we shouldn't use a van at all. What about the other ideas?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, precisely. The vehicle is a liability. I need to see if the grant structure allows us to avoid that recurring cost entirely.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the vehicle issue is real, but my records show a different gap. We have the tradespeople, but no one trained to supervise them.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: @Minako, that supervision gap is exactly the kind of hidden cost that sinks good intentions.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: @Minako, that is a critical oversight. We cannot assume supervision exists just because the tools do.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"- **Rin**: @Minako, but the evening bookings are full and people use the catalogue late! Why do we lock up when they are still there?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, the late demand is real, but it doesn't solve the supervision gap Minako identified. We need a solution that fits our current staffing reality.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Rin, the late demand is real, but it doesn't solve the supervision gap I identified. We need a solution that fits our current staffing reality.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: @Benjamin, I agree. We must choose a path that does not depend on conditions we cannot control, like weather or grant renewals.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: @Shizue, the road closures prove physical barriers are real, but the bus loss is the deeper wound. We must reach those cut off.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"- **Rin**: @Jonathan, but the halls kept their evening timetapes even when the roads were shut! So people still want to come, right?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, the halls kept their timetables, yes, but that proves local resilience, not that our central budget can sustain it.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Jonathan, the bus loss is severe, but we cannot fix infrastructure. We must pick a service that fits our current, limited supervisory capacity.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
